      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "Implement and run the numerical experiment to test Hypothesis 1 (Computation/Approximation Bounds). The experiment will scan constraint sample counts w ∈ {10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 500, 1000} and hidden widths N ∈ {4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256}. For each (w, N) pair, train a single-hidden-layer ReLU network on f(x) = sin(2πx) + 0.5 sin(6πx) with MAE loss using Adam (lr=1e-3) for 10,000 epochs with 5 random initializations. Determine N_c(w) as the minimum N achieving zero violation (max test MAE ≤ 1e-3 on 100 held-out points). Analyze the scaling of N_c(w) to distinguish between linear, constant, and logarithmic growth."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "ml_experimental_design"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "N_c(w) will exhibit linear scaling with w (N_c ∝ w), supporting Hypothesis 1. Specifically, N_c values will increase monotonically with w, with N_c(10) ≈ 4-8 and N_c(1000) ≈ 128-256, showing clear linear trend rather than constant or logarithmic behavior."
    },
